<title>FRANCE: CGE unit wins contracts for 1.45 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>CGE unit wins contracts for 1.45 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Water, an Australian-based subsidiary of Cie Generale des Eaux (CGE), has won two water contracts in New Zealand and Indonesia for a total of 1.45 billion francs, CGE said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that United Water had won a 1.2 billion franc contract to provide drinking water to the Papakura suburb of Auckland and a 300 million franc contract to build wells and provide drinking water for Sidoarjo, a city in Java.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
